# Product URLs vs delivery region

Each product has one indexable URL per language:

- `/en/catalog/[slug]`
- `/th/catalog/[slug]`
- `/zh-hk/catalog/[slug]`

The catalog listing also has one URL per language: `/[lang]/catalog`.

The selected delivery region is **not** part of the product or catalog-listing path. Store it in:

- cookie `lanna-bloom-delivery-region` (`DeliveryDestinationId`)
- existing market session (`lanna-bloom-delivery-market`)

Product pages, cards, and feeds must link to the clean catalog slug. Middleware 308s `/[lang]/catalog/[region]/[slug]` onto the clean URL and sets the cookie.

City catalog listings `/[lang]/catalog/[market]` also **308** onto `/[lang]/catalog` and set the cookie. Internal shop CTAs must use `/[lang]/catalog`, never `/catalog/phuket`.

City landings `/[lang]/[market]/flower-delivery` stay live for customers and ads. They are **operational**, not SEO pages, unless `seoIndexable` is explicitly true. Default: `noindex, follow`, omitted from the sitemap. Do not `robots.txt` Disallow them. Do not 301 them while they still serve customers/ads.

Do **not**:

- Reintroduce `/[lang]/catalog/[region]/[slug]` in internal links, sitemap, canonicals, or hreflang
- Reintroduce indexable `/[lang]/catalog/[market]` listings
- Put regional product URLs in JSON-LD `url`
- Put expansion city names in `/catalog` title/canonical when the cookie is another city
- Clear the region cookie when loading a clean product page or the main catalog listing

Checkout must recompute price and availability from catalog + destination. Never trust a client-submitted price.
